cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Post-adsorption phage resistance in Escherichia: a re-analysis of the
  Picard and Guelin phage-host interaction collection
message: >-
  If you use this analysis or its code, please cite it, and cite the
  upstream data separately using the references listed below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hussain
    given-names: Qasim
    email: qasimhussain6798@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  A re-analysis of a species-wide Escherichia phage-host interaction screen
  asking how many intracellular defense systems remain associated with
  resisting infection once the phage tested, the host surface it must bind
  and the clonal lineage of the host are all held fixed. Associations are
  estimated with cluster-robust and stratified models, stressed against
  phylogenetically matched and clonally matched null traits, extended to the
  whole accessory genome without a catalogue, and resolved phage by phage.
  Negative and null results are reported with the same prominence as positive
  ones. The output is a ranked list of candidates for knockout experiments
  rather than a demonstration that any system confers resistance.
keywords:
  - bacteriophage
  - Escherichia coli
  - anti-phage defense systems
  - phage-host interaction
  - population structure
  - comparative genomics
  - statistical genetics
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-10-16'
